{
  "rationale": "All 7 front designs are pipelined_m and the front spans only luts_plus_ffs 1219..1620 against an HV reference of 4000, with accuracy 12.9..15.1 bits against a reference of 12 — i.e. the front covers only a small slice of the luts_plus_ffs objective range, exactly the condition for a full-front mapping round. The trade-off curve is clearly under-sampled: the best accuracy seen (16.56 bits) is not on the front, and pipelined's best feasible luts_plus_ffs (1723) is worse than pipelined_m's 1219, so the two families on the front have not been jointly mapped. The throughput constraint (>=32 MSPS) is met by every evaluation (best 273), while the binding constraints are accuracy (46% violate) and sys_p99_batch_us (36% violate, best 0.158 vs 0.44) — so the feasible region is defined by accuracy/system timing, not throughput, and iterative/unrolled_k (N+3 and ceil(N/k)+3 cycles/result, well under 32 MSPS at these N) cannot enter the front. With 100 of 200 evals left, the best use is to let NSGA-II map the whole front over the full ranges of pipelined and pipelined_m, seeded with the current front, rather than narrowing around a 7-point slice.",
  "next_plan": null,
  "decision": "map_front"
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget is exhausted (200/200 evals, round 3 of 4 complete), so this is the terminal decision point. The spec is feasible, not infeasible: all three constraints are met with margin by designs on the front — throughput_msps best 273 vs >=32 (0% violations), max_abs_err best 3.14e-08 vs <=2.44e-04 (2^-12), and sys_p99_batch_us best 0.158 us vs <=0.44 us. The feasible front is well populated (90 feasible / 78 unique, 18 Pareto designs) and spans luts_plus_ffs 1211..3705 against the HV reference 4000, with accuracy_bits 12..22.2 against reference 12, i.e. it covers both objective ranges rather than a single corner, and hypervolume improved +29.3% this round. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) lands on pipelined_m [W=15 N=15 angle_guard=2 frac_guard=4 round m=4] at luts_plus_ffs=1211, accuracy_bits=12.03 (max_abs_err 2.40e-04, just inside the 2^-12 limit) and throughput 93.6 MSPS, comfortably above the 32 MSPS floor. The only residual risk is that this cheapest design's sys_p99_batch_us margin is an L1 analytic bound and will be re-checked by L2 simulation, but that re-selection is handled by code after this loop, and no further exploration budget remains to change the front. Stopping is therefore the correct terminal action."
